From 5eec680783b4b151becbb94bba799be781149887 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sjcsf <346224915+llsf2020@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/19] FreeChat: strict mode; messages do not outlive the
 process

Strict mode (per device, opt-in): the session is kept in memory only, its SDK
stores are encrypted with a key that never leaves memory and deleted on the
next start, it signs out after the chosen time in the background, and password
sign-ins use a device ID the homeserver removes once idle. In every mode the
event and media caches are dropped whenever a session's client is created.
